  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) TCA 2-7-112(c), new subdivision (number left blank '(_)'), Section 2\n(quote) An employee identification card for retired state employees authorized pursuant to § 8-50-118;\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) Sec 1: new TCA 8-50-118: 'The state shall allow an employee upon retirement to keep such employee's employee photo identification card issued by the state. A sticker or other designation shall be placed on the employee photo identification card to indicate that the employee is retired.'\n(other) Sec 3: effective on becoming law.\n(other) version: Draft (only version saved): adds retired state employee ID cards to the 2-7-112(c) list (slot a). The enrolled and chaptered (Public Chapter 938) texts are not saved, so changes made after filing cannot be checked.\n(other) note: Title says 'As enacted'. Subdivision number in Draft is blank '(_)'. No amendment recorded in the actions. House passage was on a companion bill substituted for it.",
